From: Synkar <dev@synkar.com>
Subject: [PATCH] bcmdhd: demote "No WPSIE in beacon" log to debug

wl_cfg80211_hostapd_sec() logs an error every beacon refresh (~6 s) when
the AP beacon carries no WPS IE, but a WPS IE is optional (hostapd does
not add one unless configured). The same condition is already logged at
debug level in the beacon parse path. Demote to WL_DBG to stop the
kernel log spam; nothing else changes.

--- a/wl_cfgvif.c
+++ b/wl_cfgvif.c
@@ -4062,7 +4062,7 @@
 			}
 		}
 	} else {
-		WL_ERR(("No WPSIE in beacon \n"));
+		WL_DBG(("No WPSIE in beacon \n"));
 	}
 	return 0;
 }
